      "evidence": "The statement allows arbitrary supplied rank-zero R-orientations, but step 4.1 asserts e=1 and identity cup maps. The opened Euler-class definition gives e(0_B,o)=o. For B a point, R=Z and o=-1, the Euler class is -1 and cup multiplication is -id. Retain the supplied orientation unit or restrict this sentence to the standard orientation. The assigned consumer reaches this supplier through thm-mod-two-euler-class-is-the-top-stiefel-whitney-class; its canonical mod-two application is unaffected.",
